<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spartacist uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as January uprising</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spartacist uprising was a general strike and armed rising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> from 5 to 12 January 1919, led by the newly founded Communist Party of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and other radicals against the Social Democratic government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-ebert">Friedrich Ebert</a>. It was crushed by army units and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freikorps">Freikorps</a> sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-noske">Gustav Noske</a>, and the communist leaders Rosa Luxemburg and Karl Liebknecht were murdered on 15 January.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spartacist-uprising.jpg" alt="Spartacist uprising" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: New-York Tribune · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soldiers_the_Brandenburger_Tor_during_the_Spartacist_uprising_Jan_7_1919.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
